(Discrepancy 4: LANGUAGE.md:686-688 says a bare identifier "is not a reserved
 keyword" and that "reserved keywords remain rejected as names". A for-range
 loop variable may be a reserved keyword: `For each number from 1 to 3`
 compiles and binds `number`, while `a number called number is 5.` is
 rejected (VAR-54). The generator already relies on this — src/gen_flow.vox
 lines 426 and 434 emit exactly this loop — so it is live in every campaign.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D4.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   1
   2
   3
)
For each number from 1 to 3, Print number.
